From 81df3ace4244a68164aa8ff18081461ab3e28281 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:53:05 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(setup): per-setup post options and the setup's own
 tool-list export
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A setup's post options (skip pauses and homes, one file per operation,
thread output) follow the document's until the setup's Post page gives
it its own - the #343 own / follow-the-document law. SetupDef gains
post_options: Option<PostOptions>, set by the new undoable
SetSetupPostOptions; the option widgets route to the active setup's own
options when it has them, else to the document's SetPostOptions. Each
operation posts with its own setup's skip switch; the Output and thread
output are the active setup's, and a program whose setups disagree on
them is refused by name in the verification gate. The setup's options
save as an additive SetupDto key (absent = follows), so documents that
never set them save and post byte for byte as before.

The setup's Tool list page gains "Export tool list…": the setup's tools
(T number, name, diameter, kind, holder, operations) as RFC 4180 CSV or
plain text by the chosen extension, built by app::tool_list_export (a
pure read) and written by the UI without touching the history.

Fixes #389

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
